# Deny by default, then allow only what the extension needs at runtime.
#
# The packer (@anthropic-ai/mcpb) uses the `ignore` library, so this file has gitignore
# semantics: "/*" excludes every top-level entry, and "!/name" re-includes one. It packs
# the working directory and does not read .gitignore, so with a blocklist any untracked
# local directory ends up in the bundle. The first v4.1.0 asset shipped a scratch
# directory with files named "review-<sha>..<sha>.diff" and Claude Desktop refused to
# install it (path traversal check). A bare "dist" rule in the old blocklist also matched
# node_modules/*/dist and stripped the SDK's compiled files.
#
# `npm run verify:mcpb` checks the packed bundle against this same list.

/*

# Runtime
!/build
!/node_modules
!/package.json
!/manifest.json

# Shown in Claude Desktop
!/img
!/README.md
!/LICENSE

# Never needed at runtime even though the directories above are allowed
/node_modules/.bin
/node_modules/.cache
/build/*.map
